  "question": {
    "text": "If the point of intersection of the plane <math><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> with the line through the origin and perpendicular to the plane <math><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>, then the distance of the point <math><mi>P</mi></math> from <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is",
